      "category": "process",
      "threshold": "100% of infrastructure pull requests show the monthly cost change; above {{COST_STEP}} a month the check fails until the pull request carries the label budget-approved",
      "description": "Infracost compares the cost of the pull request's Terraform with the main branch and comments the difference; the step then fails above the limit unless the budget owner has added the label budget-approved, which only they may add (a CODEOWNERS-protected label rule or a workflow that checks who added it).\n\nTool: Infracost with the GitHub CLI\n\n```bash\ninfracost breakdown --path . --format json --out-file base.json        # run on the main branch checkout\ninfracost diff --path . --compare-to base.json --format json --out-file diff.json\ninfracost comment github --path diff.json --repo \"$GITHUB_REPOSITORY\" \\\n  --pull-request \"$PR_NUMBER\" --github-token \"$GITHUB_TOKEN\" --behavior update\nincrease=$(jq -r '(.diffTotalMonthlyCost // \"0\") | tonumber | floor' diff.json)\napproved=$(gh pr view \"$PR_NUMBER\" --json labels -q '.labels[].name' | grep -cx budget-approved || true)\n[ \"$increase\" -le {{COST_STEP}} ] || [ \"$approved\" -gt 0 ] \\\n  || { echo \"adds $increase a month: the budget owner adds the label budget-approved\"; exit 1; }\n```",
      "hubWhen": {
        "IAC": [
          "terraform"
        ],
        "CLOUD": [
          "aws",
          "azure",
          "gcp"
        ]
      }
    },
