    {
      "id": "ff-kube-score",
      "type": "fitness-fn",
      "label": "Manifests well specified",
      "x": 1040,
      "y": 2080,
      "category": "structural",
      "threshold": "0 critical kube-score findings in the rendered manifests (CPU and memory requests, memory limit, probes, replicas, PodDisruptionBudget, non-root user and group, read-only root file system, and kube-score's correctness checks), with the default checks the requirement does not ask for switched off",
      "description": "The rendered manifests of every chart or overlay are scored in each pull request; a critical finding fails the build. The chart renders its PodDisruptionBudget with the Deployment, so the deployment-has-poddisruptionbudget check sees both; the user-and-group and read-only-root-file-system checks are on by default in current kube-score. The defaults that ask for more than the requirement (a CPU limit, ephemeral-storage requests and limits, pull policy Always, a NetworkPolicy per pod, host anti-affinity) are switched off; network reachability is not decided in this pack.\n\nTool: kube-score\n\n```bash\nhelm template order-api charts/order-api -f charts/order-api/values-production.yaml \\\n  | kube-score score - --output-format ci \\\n      --ignore-container-cpu-limit \\\n      --ignore-test container-ephemeral-storage-request-and-limit \\\n      --ignore-test container-image-pull-policy \\\n      --ignore-test pod-networkpolicy \\\n      --ignore-test deployment-has-host-podantiaffinity \\\n      --ignore-test statefulset-has-host-podantiaffinity\n```",
      "hubWhen": {
        "HOSTING": [
          "kubernetes"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ff-kube-score-onprem",
      "type": "fitness-fn",
      "label": "Manifests well specified",
      "x": 1040,
      "y": 2210,
      "category": "structural",
      "threshold": "0 critical kube-score findings in the rendered manifests (CPU and memory requests, memory limit, probes, replicas, PodDisruptionBudget, non-root user and group, read-only root file system, and kube-score's correctness checks), with the default checks the requirement does not ask for switched off",
      "description": "The rendered manifests of every chart or overlay are scored in each pull request; a critical finding fails the build. The chart renders its PodDisruptionBudget with the Deployment, so the deployment-has-poddisruptionbudget check sees both; the user-and-group and read-only-root-file-system checks are on by default in current kube-score. The defaults that ask for more than the requirement (a CPU limit, ephemeral-storage requests and limits, pull policy Always, a NetworkPolicy per pod, host anti-affinity) are switched off; network reachability is not decided in this pack.\n\nTool: kube-score\n\n```bash\nhelm template order-api charts/order-api -f charts/order-api/values-production.yaml \\\n  | kube-score score - --output-format ci \\\n      --ignore-container-cpu-limit \\\n      --ignore-test container-ephemeral-storage-request-and-limit \\\n      --ignore-test container-image-pull-policy \\\n      --ignore-test pod-networkpolicy \\\n      --ignore-test deployment-has-host-podantiaffinity \\\n      --ignore-test statefulset-has-host-podantiaffinity\n```",
      "hubWhen": {
        "HOSTING": [
